<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Falaise</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1174</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falaise">Falaise</a> was imposed in December 1174 on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-lion">William the Lion</a>, King of Scots, who had been captured at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alnwick">Alnwick</a> while invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. William accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> as his feudal overlord and handed over the castles of Roxburgh, Berwick, Jedburgh, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> cancelled the treaty in 1189 in return for 10,000 marks, by the Quitclaim of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-falaise.jpg" alt="Treaty of Falaise" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: rene boulay · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calvados_Falaise_Chateau_041996_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
